 card("**Skills at work, not re-taught here.** *Mating patterns* (the final mate with a bishop defended by a rook), *Double check* and *Discovered attacks and checks* (10.Bg5+), *Types of sacrifice* (the queen given up for mate), *Searching for a forced mate* (all three finishing moves were checks). Our reading: move 8 prepared it, because castling put the rook on d1 behind its own bishop and queen. That is a reading of the position, not a claim about what either player thought."),
 dict(type="reflect", kind="unsure", prompt="Which of the five moments (7.Bd2, 8.O-O-O, 9.Qd8+, 10.Bg5+, 11.Bd8#) would you have missed in a game of your own, and what would you have had to notice?",
  fields=[dict(id="missed", label="The moment I would have missed:", options=["7.Bd2", "8.O-O-O", "9.Qd8+", "10.Bg5+", "11.Bd8#", "none of them"]),
          dict(id="notice", label="What I would have needed to notice:", options=["a check that leaves one reply", "a piece that blocks its own rook", "a file that opens when a piece moves", "the king's own pieces blocking it", "something else"])]),
